# Trivy vulnerability exceptions for the must-gather image
#
# BR-SECURITY-2493 / DD-PLATFORM-003: explicit user-approved risk acceptance
# on 2026-10-11, expiring 2027-04-11 (six calendar months). Owner: Kubernaut
# Platform Team. Tracked in Issue #1662; delivered with PR #2493.
# This is risk acceptance, not vulnerability remediation.
#
# The installed kubectl remains v1.36.2 (Go 1.26.4, x/net v0.49.0,
# x/text v0.33.0). Trivy v0.72.0 / DB 2026-10-11 reported 19 HIGH package
# findings / 16 unique CVEs in this binary. Renew the 13 expired entries
# and add only the three newly observed IDs (78667, 78669, 97031).
#
# Checksum-verified published kubectl v1.36.5 and v1.37.1 fix 13 of these
# CVEs but still report the three new HIGH IDs. Retaining the current binary
# and accepting even the already-addressed upstream findings is deliberate;
# do not claim that fixes are unavailable or that this image is CVE-free.
# An isolated patched source-build spike was clean, but that new production
# build strategy was not selected. No kubectl version/build change is made.
#
# CI/release route this file only to the must-gather image, never application
# service images or govulncheck. Trivy severities, exit codes, and discovery
# remain unchanged; unlisted CVEs still fail the image gate.
#
# Re-run before the expiration date:
#   1. Inspect released binaries with `go version -m` and real binary scans
#      (current minimum fixes: Go 1.26.9, x/net v0.60.0, x/text v0.39.0).
#   2. Validate any replacement against the documented collector/server
#      compatibility contract, then remove resolved exceptions early.
#   3. Re-triage Issue #1662. Renewal requires fresh explicit risk approval;
#      expiration must resurface these findings, not silently renew them.

